Please target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nThis introduces support for `XR_EXT_spatial_container` & `XR_EXT_spatial_container_self_rendering`, newly ratified OpenXR multi-vendor (EXT) extensions, that defines the new **OpenXR Multi-App paradigm**.\r\n\r\nIn this new paradigm, OpenXR introduces **Spatial Containers**, an abstraction for an OpenXR application to render into a shared scene via a bounded or unbounded volume in space, allowing OpenXR applications to multi-task alongside other spatial container and / or regular applications.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1437\" height=\"809\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-02 at 6 16 59 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa281c1e-fb36-4d26-aea4-695dc5078d77\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFor more info about OpenXR Multi-App, please take a look at the SIGGRAPH 2026 [talk](https://youtu.be/V68nO3Vxok8?t=3078&si=HIVgYeXJhv8qBtTk) and [slides](https://www.khronos.org/assets/uploads/developers/presentations/OpenXR_BOF_v2_SIGG_2026_-_Slides.pdf):\r\n\r\n**Note:** Keeping in draft until https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123123 is merged.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"ht